{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1399","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Binary String To Subsequences"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a binary string $$$s$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ zeros and ones."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to divide the given string into the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subsequences"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in such a way that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"each character"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the string belongs to exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"one subsequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and each subsequence looks like \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"010101 ..."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"101010 ..."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (i.e. the subsequence should not contain two adjacent zeros or ones)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall that a subsequence is a sequence that can be derived from the given sequence by deleting zero or more elements without changing the order of the remaining elements. For example, subsequences of \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1011101"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"101"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1001"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", but not \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"000"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"101010"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to answer $$$t$$$ independent test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2 \\cdot 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. Then $$$t$$$ test cases follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the test case contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of $$$s$$$. The second line of the test case contains $$$n$$$ characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' — the string $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$ ($$$\\sum n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the answer: in the first line print one integer $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le n$$$) — the minimum number of subsequences you can divide the string $$$s$$$ to. In the second line print $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le k$$$), where $$$a_i$$$ is the number of subsequence the $$$i$$$-th character of $$$s$$$ belongs to."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are several answers, you can print any."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n4\n0011\n6\n111111\n5\n10101\n8\n01010000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1 2 2 1 \n6\n1 2 3 4 5 6 \n1\n1 1 1 1 1 \n4\n1 1 1 1 1 2 3 4 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1399D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1399/problem/D"}